// spec: TYP-013
//
// TYP-013 requires a type name to denote a declared type, so this program must
// be refused when it is read.  The name is never resolved instead: the test is
// silently false, the guarded branch never runs, and the program reports
// success.
//
// ⚠️ 'is' is uniquely permissive about its right-hand side.  The same undefined
// name used as a VALUE is 'Undefined variable', which is what makes this an
// inconsistency rather than a general looseness about names.

WriteLn (1 is Nonexistent);

if 1 is Integr then
    WriteLn ('misspelled Integer took the then branch');
else
    WriteLn ('misspelled Integer silently took the else branch');
